Package: CODAC
Type: Package
Title: Circadian Oscillation Detection, Analysis and Comparison
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Thiago", "Parente da Silveira", email = "thiago.silveira@gp.ita.br", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Leonardo Vinicius", "Monteiro de Assis", role = "aut"))
Description: A unified framework for detecting, characterizing and comparing
    circadian rhythmicity in biological time-series data. CODAC bundles four
    tools that share one Python analysis engine, wrapped in R via reticulate:
    codac_single() for fixed-period rhythmicity estimation in a single group;
    codac_flex() for flexible waveform-model selection (standard, linear, damped,
    rapidly damped); codac_compare() for pairwise differential rhythmicity between
    two or more groups; and codac_multi() for the multi-group grouping question,
    selecting the best configuration of rhythm (and, separately, baseline) sharing
    across groups by model selection. The Python engine and its dependencies are
    set up automatically on first use.
